{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לא הביט און ביעקב", :translit "lo hebit aven be-ya'akov", :gloss "He has not beheld iniquity in Jacob"} {:he "שאין אותיות חט בשמותיהן של שבטים", :translit "she-ein otiot chet-tet be-shemoteihen shel shevatim", :gloss "for the letters chet-tet are not in the names of the tribes"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The two-letter sequence חט (chet-tet) never appears in any tribal name: Reuven, Shimon, Levi, Yehudah, Yissachar, Zevulun, Dan, Yosef, Binyamin, Naftali, Gad, Asher, Yissachar — none contain consecutive chet-tet."}], :frame {:text "Bil'am's prophecy in Numbers 23:21 declares that God beholds no iniquity (און) in Jacob. The Ba'al HaTurim notes a graphic curiosity: scanning the names of the twelve tribes (Genesis 49:3-27 for the sons of Jacob, or Numbers 1:5-15 for the tribal leaders), the consecutive letters ח and ט never appear, reinforcing the verse's message that sin is absent from Israel.", :sources ["Numbers 23:21" "Genesis 49:3-27" "Numbers 1:5-15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The two-letter sequence חט (chet-tet) never appears in any tribal name: Reuven, Shimon, Levi, Yehudah, Yissachar, Zevulun, Dan, Yosef, Binyamin, Naftali, Gad, Asher, Yissachar — none contain consecutive chet-tet.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:59.196100877Z", :model "glm-5.2"}